# netsurf: an :empty flip a sibling rule could see rebuilds the parent (patch 450)
# Generated 2026-11-25
# Base: seleron/vitabrowser (patch stack through 449)
#
# "a sibling rule tests :empty" (patch 373's html_rl_empty_sibling_risk, at
# 440's html_rl_block_whole, 438's html_rl_flex_whole and the two line-path
# checks of 373: a line emptied, content arriving in an empty block) was
# the census's largest local decline after 447/448 (4.0 a load on the 7
# sites). A + / ~ rule whose left compound has :empty reaches only the
# block's later siblings and their descendants, all inside its parent;
# :has() never matches here (patch 328) and no ancestor can flip :empty
# (each holds the block). So the parent is built again whole --
# html_rl_parent_whole, factored out of 445's html_rl_sib_parent_rebuild:
# a block (440) or a flex or grid box (438), one level only (a depth
# guard) -- and only a parent that cannot be keeps the decline.
#
